    "https://jobsearch.london.edu/jobs/8262304-database-manager": {
      "title": "Database Manager",
      "description": "Database Manager - London Business School This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Skip to main content Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Advancement · London Business School, London · Hybrid Database Manager Apply for this job Enable data‑driven alumni engagement at a world‑leading business school Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. The Role London Business School is seeking a Database Manager to play a key role in enabling effective alumni engagement and philanthropic activity through high‑quality data, systems and insight. This role sits within the Advancement team and focuses on maximising the value of our core fundraising and alumni database (currently Raiser’s Edge) to support strategic growth and engagement. You will work closely with colleagues across Advancement to ensure our data systems are robust, well‑governed and easy to use, enabling teams to build meaningful, life‑long relationships with alumni, donors and supporters. You will provide end‑to‑end database capability to support the Advancement department and wider School community. You will manage system configuration, data quality, reporting and user support, ensuring colleagues can confidently use data and fundraising tools to deliver their objectives. A key part of the role is supporting and developing colleagues through training and guidance, acting as a subject‑matter expert on Raiser’s Edge and related systems, and helping shape future system enhancements as the department’s needs evolve. Main Responsibilities Manage and maintain the Advancement database (currently Raiser’s Edge), ensuring data accuracy, integrity and effective use. Deliver database training and documentation for new and existing users, including ongoing \"top up\" training. Analyse changing requirements and support system upgrades and enhancements in collaboration with the Head of Data. Provide reporting and ad hoc data analysis to support fundraising, engagement and decision making. Act as the first point of contact for complex data issues, identifying problems, proposing solutions and maintaining issue logs. Support data governance, data privacy and information security in line with School policies and committee requirements. Mentor and support the Data Coordinator, enabling skills development and timely data provision across Advancement. Contribute to School wide information systems initiatives, including data maturity improvements. Who We Are Looking For Experience working with relational databases, ideally within a fundraising or CRM environment (e.g. Raiser’s Edge). Experience of database requirements analysis, upgrades or system improvements. Strong analytical skills with the ability to produce clear, accurate reports. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with confidence delivering training to diverse audiences. Advanced Microsoft Excel skills; knowledge of query tools such as SQL is desirable. Strong attention to detail and ability to manage confidential or sensitive data. Ability to prioritise work effectively and operate with a high level of autonomy. A collaborative, customer focused approach and strong relationship building skills. Benefits You Can Enjoy Generous annual leave of 27 days plus extra days between Christmas and New Year USS pension, 14.5% employer contribution (in return for employee enrolment and contribution) Free onsite gym and swimming pool Amazing range of professional development to support your career path Enhanced cycle to work scheme Wellbeing offering to support your physical, mental and financial health At London Business School, we support Smart Working - a hybrid approach designed to help you achieve a healthy work-life balance while delivering the best outcomes for your role and the needs of our customers. All roles require a minimum of two days on campus each week to foster a vibrant, collaborative community. For this role specifically, you will be expected to be on campus 2 days per week. We operate with ‘core hours’ – 10:00-15:00 – to maximise opportunities for connection and collaboration across teams during the working day. Outside of these hours, you may still be required for meetings or collaboration based on your role and customer needs. Additionally, we offer Protected Time - a flexible, one-hour slot, within the working week dedicated to your learning and development, wellbeing, or focused, quiet work Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description View London Business School Benefits Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: 7th September 2026 Department Advancement Locations London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Advancement · London Business School, London · Hybrid Database Manager Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobsearch.london.edu/jobs/8253427-senior-finance-business-partner": {
      "title": "Senior Finance Business Partner",
      "description": "Senior Finance Business Partner - London Business School This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Skip to main content Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Finance · London Business School, London · Hybrid Senior Finance Business Partner Apply for this job Partner with senior leaders to shape strategic decision-making through insight, robust forecasting and high-quality financial advice. Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. The Role London Business School is looking for an experienced and commercially minded Senior Finance Business Partner to join our Finance team. Working within Financial Planning & Analysis, you will provide a full finance business partnering service to key operational and commercial functions across the School. You will play an important role in supporting strategic and operational decision-making through insightful analysis, robust forecasting, high-quality reporting and trusted financial advice. As a senior member of the FP&A leadership team, you will work closely with senior stakeholders across the School, including the CFO, Deputy CFO, senior leadership colleagues, Finance leaders and wider management teams. You will lead the coordination and delivery of long-term plans, annual budgets and periodic forecasts, while ensuring business stakeholders are fully engaged and supported. This is an opportunity to contribute directly to the School’s medium and long-term strategy by helping colleagues understand performance, identify opportunities, manage resources effectively and make well-informed decisions. Main Responsibilities Act as a senior member of the FP&A leadership team, providing financial insight suitable for senior executive audiences. Lead the coordination and delivery of long-term plans, annual budgets and periodic forecasts, ensuring strong engagement with business stakeholders. Provide day-to-day financial support to senior managers, ensuring accurate and timely reporting of revenue, costs and performance. Develop and maintain financial models to support strategic planning, scenario analysis and business case development. Support new initiatives, commercial opportunities and strategic projects through high-quality financial advice and analysis. Manage a small team to ensure high-quality analysis, reporting and workload delivery. Partner with relevant areas to understand their business goals and provide professional advice, technical expertise and financial information to support effective decision-making. Extract, check and analyse data from multiple sources, producing reports that inform review, planning and management decisions. Liaise across Finance and the wider School to prepare complex reports and support cross-functional planning. Provide advice on policies, procedures and compliance requirements, supporting monitoring and assurance across the School. Monitor work delivered by third-party suppliers and agencies where relevant, ensuring agreed service levels and quality standards are met. Build strong relationships with stakeholders across the School and represent Finance on cross-School groups where required. Lead or support projects within your area of expertise, ensuring delivery within agreed budgets, quality standards and timescales. Contribute to process improvement by reviewing best practice, analysing business models and helping develop policies, processes and systems. Champion change by role-modelling expected behaviours, advising on change programmes and supporting successful implementation. Who We Are Looking For A professional accounting qualification, or equivalent experience. Significant experience using relevant software to build basic financial models or tools. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. Strong communication skills, with the ability to engage a wide range of audiences and explain financial information clearly. Sound working knowledge of relevant policies, regulations and legislation within a finance or specialist area. The ability to manage multiple internal and external stakeholders effectively. The ability to prioritise and focus on material issues in a busy environment. In-depth knowledge of business education or a relevant specialist area. Experience leading projects and supporting change. Experience managing external suppliers or contractors effectively. Strong financial management experience and commercial acumen. The confidence to work with senior leaders and provide constructive challenge where needed. A collaborative, service-focused approach and commitment to continuous improvement. Benefits You Can Enjoy Generous annual leave of 27 days plus extra days between Christmas and New Year USS pension, 14.5% employer contribution (in return for employee enrolment and contribution) Free onsite gym and swimming pool Amazing range of professional development to support your career path Enhanced cycle to work scheme Wellbeing offering to support your physical, mental and financial health At London Business School, we support Smart Working - a hybrid approach designed to help you achieve a healthy work-life balance while delivering the best outcomes for your role and the needs of our customers. All roles require a minimum of two days on campus each week to foster a vibrant, collaborative community. For this role specifically, you will be expected to be on campus x days per week. We operate with ‘core hours’ – 10:00-15:00 – to maximise opportunities for connection and collaboration across teams during the working day. Outside of these hours, you may still be required for meetings or collaboration based on your role and customer needs. Additionally, we offer Protected Time - a flexible, one-hour slot, within the working week dedicated to your learning and development, wellbeing, or focused, quiet work Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description View London Business School Benefits Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: Friday 4th September 2026 Department Finance Locations London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Finance · London Business School, London · Hybrid Senior Finance Business Partner Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
